marian-dev 2781d73: faiss/VectorTransform.cpp includes no SSE header.

The file uses __m128 and _mm_* under `#ifdef __SSE__` but never includes
<xmmintrin.h>; it relied on a header that an x86 Linux toolchain pulled in
transitively. With the Android NDK for x86_64 the macro is set and the types
are missing, so Marian did not compile for x86_64. The header is now included
under the same condition (x86 targets only). Nothing changes for ARM, where
__SSE__ is not defined. __SSE3__ (for _mm_hadd_ps) is set by the x86_64
baseline the NDK uses.

Licence: modification of Marian (MIT), under the same licence.
Applied by scripts/sources.py with patch -p1 from the marian-dev root.

--- a/src/3rd_party/faiss/VectorTransform.cpp
+++ b/src/3rd_party/faiss/VectorTransform.cpp
@@ -13,6 +13,10 @@
 #include <cmath>
 #include <cstring>
 #include <memory>
+
+#ifdef __SSE__
+#include <pmmintrin.h>
+#endif
 
 #include <faiss/utils/random.h>
 #include "common/logging.h"
